# Privacy compliance — safe rollout (web → hybrid native → multi-country)

Design notes only. Resume: `@privacy-compliance$`.

**Production host (cutover):** see `.cursor/rules/cutoffrequirement.mdc` — canonical origin is `https://www.floqr.com` (may be prepared before DNS flip).

Not legal advice. Goal: raise GDPR / CCPA / Consent Mode posture **without breaking** signed-in product flows (Mingl, Search, ShoutOut, scheduling, ads rotation, SOS2FA).

## Constraint: what “without breaking” means

| Safe (additive) | Risky if done naively |
|---|---|
| Privacy Policy page + links | Tightening `users` read to owner-only (Mingl/Search/admin may list peers today) |
| Expand export fields via callable | Defaulting all notify/marketing OFF overnight for existing users |
| Honor GPC into a new flag (ads later) | Deleting Auth users without Storage/Firestore cascade |
| Consent Mode defaults **only if** `gtag` exists | Blocking App Check / phone reCAPTCHA (auth breaks) |
| Gate **new** marketing sends on consent | Rewriting profile schema mid-flight |

**Rule:** prefer new collections / callables / flags with **grandfather defaults** that preserve current behavior until an explicit migration cutover.

## Architecture for hybrid native (Capacitor / similar)

Do **not** build cookie-only compliance. Shared privacy core:

| Layer | Module (proposed) | Web | Hybrid native |
|---|---|---|---|
| Preferences | `floqr-privacy-prefs.js` | localStorage + `users` fields | Same Firestore fields; Capacitor Preferences as cache |
| Policy / DNS | `privacy.html` + in-app WebView or native screen | `?v=` pages | Bundled HTML or remote URL; App Store / Play links |
| Signals | `floqr-privacy-signals.js` | GPC header / `navigator.globalPrivacyControl` | iOS ATT (`AppTrackingTransparency`); Android Play Data Safety; no cookie banner as sole control |
| Analytics gate | `floqr-consent-mode.js` | Consent Mode v2 before gtag | Firebase Analytics / ATT before IDFA; same preference keys |
| DSAR | Cloud Functions | HTTPS / callable | Same callables from native |

**Shared preference keys (already partially exist):**  
`marketingConsent`, `analyticsConsent`, `dataSharingConsent`, `publicMinglDatapoints`, plus proposed: `doNotSellOrShare`, `gpcAppliedAt`, `privacyPolicyVersionAccepted`, `privacyRegion` (`eu`|`us-ca`|`us`|`br`|…).

## Multi-country (eventual)

| Region | Minimum product behavior |
|---|---|
| EU/EEA/UK | Art. 13 notice, lawful basis labels, real erasure, CMP before non-essential cookies/SDK |
| California (CPRA) | Notice at collection, Do Not Sell/Share, GPC |
| Brazil (LGPD) | Similar notice + rights; Portuguese pack already in i18n |
| Other | Same privacy core; locale packs for policy + My Privacy (floqr-i18n) |

Region detection: profile `country` / `uiLanguage` + IP country **only as hint** — never silent consent. Prefer user-confirmed region on first privacy gate.

## Phased work I can do in-repo (safe order)

### Phase A — Additive notice (no behavior change)
1. `privacy.html` (controller placeholder, purposes, processors list from code: Firebase, Twilio, SendGrid, Stripe, Google reCAPTCHA/Places, retention pointers).
2. Links from My Privacy, Search footer/chrome, onboarding — `FLOQRNav.appVersion` cache-bust.
3. FloqAi help + design note (this file). Master Admin–only English OK; patron chrome/links i18n when shipping policy body.

### Phase B — Consent enforcement with grandfathering
1. Marketing SMS/email: require `marketingConsent === true` **OR** legacy `marketingConsent` unset **and** campaign flagged `allowLegacyUnset` until cutover date.
2. Ad personalization: if `doNotSellOrShare` or `dataSharingConsent === false` or GPC → treat as `targetMode: "all"` house creatives only / no profile tag scoring (keep ads showing, stop using PII tags).
3. Analytics: do **not** enable GA4 until Consent Mode stub + CMP; keep measurementId unused.

### Phase C — DSAR that works
1. Callable `exportPatronData` — profile + shoutouts + spotAds + consents + orders (Admin SDK).
2. Callable `fulfillPatronDelete` — master/admin or scheduled job from `deleteRequest`; soft-delete → hard purge; never leave `pending` forever.
3. Keep UI buttons; swap internals only.

### Phase D — Rules lockdown (migration required)
1. Inventory every client that reads other users’ docs (Mingl, admin lists, master diagnostics).
2. Introduce `publicProfiles/{uid}` (safe fields only) written by Cloud Function on profile save.
3. Change `users` read to `isSelf || isMasterAdmin || isClubAdminFor…`; clients switch to `publicProfiles`.
4. `privacyConsents`: create by self; read self or master; no peer update/delete.

### Phase E — CMP + Consent Mode v2 (web) / ATT (native)
1. Web: lightweight first-party CMP or vendor; defaults denied; update on choice.
2. `floqr-consent-mode.js`: if `window.gtag` exists, set denied defaults + `wait_for_update`.
3. Native: ATT prompt only if tracking; map to same `analyticsConsent` / `doNotSellOrShare`.
4. reCAPTCHA: classify as **strictly necessary security** in policy; do not block auth behind marketing CMP.

### Phase F — Hybrid packaging
1. Same privacy modules in shared JS; Capacitor shell loads them.
2. App Store privacy nutrition labels / Play Data safety aligned with actual SDKs.
3. No Xibo/`display.html` cookie banners (kiosk; public board — separate notice if needed).

## Timing vs demo / cutover

| When | What |
|---|---|
| **Now (demo on Pages)** | Ship Phases A–C: policy page, DNS/GPC, marketing grandfather gate, ad personalization soften, real DSAR export/delete, tighten `privacyConsents`. Fixes fake delete + open consents without breaking Mingl/Search. |
| **Before floqr.com cutover** | Counsel-ready controller contact on `privacy.html`; optional `privacyPolicyVersionAccepted` re-ack; App Check / OAuth host allowlists for www. |
| **At cutover** | Flip DNS; policy live at `https://www.floqr.com/privacy.html`; preview-email bases → www. |
| **After publicProfiles (Phase D)** | Lock `users` reads. Do **not** tighten peer `users` reads in the safe slice. |

